------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SCOPE / DESIGN
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web DevToolsPage is a thin tabbed shell: a PageContainer title+subtitle over
a 5-tab TabNav (Fleet API / Telemetry / Infrastructure / Utilities / Reference,
default fleet-api) that conditionally mounts one section per tab. The parity
manifest record (page:admin/DevTools) declares the unit as a shell with NO data
sources / NO panels / NO charts and requiredCount=2 (devtools.title,
devtools.subtitle).

Native implementation (SwiftUI, adaptive macOS + iOS/iPadOS, ADR-002/006):
  • DevToolsPage (View) + @Observable DevToolsPageModel — owns the active tab
    (web useUrlEnum) and the two parity strings (web usePageTitle/PageContainer).
  • TSTabs (P3 shared component) reproduces the 5-tab strip in web source order
    with SF Symbols mapped from the web lucide icons.
  • Each tab composes the existing native section surface:
        fleet-api      → FleetApiSection
        telemetry      → FleetTelemetryHealth
        infrastructure → InfrastructureSection
        utilities      → ClientUtilitiesSection
        reference      → DevToolsReferenceLinks (inline parity of
                         ReferenceLinksSection.tsx; rendered in-page to avoid a
                         top-level type collision with a sibling section prompt).
  • Sections are seeded to their honest READY/empty state (the app-wide live
    dev-tools source lands with the shared-core bridge; only InMemory sources
    exist app-wide today). Client-side Utilities (15 tools) + Reference links
    render in full — no placeholders (ADR-011).
  • Registered at the .admin route via DevToolsRouteRegistration (web /devtools
    aliases to .admin in AppRouteParser); chained into routeHosts in
    Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift (navigation registration).
  • Strings: per-surface "DevToolsPage" table (DevToolsPage.strings) resolved via
    DevToolsPageStrings.string(key, fallback); keys mirror the web t() keys.
    a11y: headers, .isLink traits, VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type (Font.TS),
    light/dark + high-contrast (generated Color.TS dynamic tokens).

